  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:8pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:8pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:8pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-top:8pt;padding-left:18pt;padding-right:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;The financial statements of Monarch Pipeline LLC (&#8220;Monarch&#8221;) are prepared in accordance with Generally Accepted Account Principles and adjusted to reflect the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accountants published accounting releases (&#8220;FERC USA&#8221;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Balance Sheet and Statement of Cash Flows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Monarch has a cash management arrangement with Williams Ohio River Valley, LLC. The cash transactions flow through the Noncurrent Assets and Noncurrent Liabilities accounts.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:107%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;Our accounting for contingencies covers a wide variety of business activities, including contingencies for legal and environmental exposures. We accrue these contingencies when our assessment indicates that it is probably that a liability has been incurred or an asset will not be recovered, and amounts can be reasonably estimated. We have no contingencies at this time&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;We have a service agreement with The Williams Companies, Inc and Williams MLP Operating, LLC under which our operations and the operations of Williams and its affiliates can combine or share certain common services in order to operate more efficiently and cost effectively. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;As a limited liability company, we do not directly pay federal income tax. Taxable income or loss is included in the federal income tax returns for the parent company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:9.67pt"&gt;None.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
